===Box office records===
* ''[[Ne Zha 2]]'' surpassed ''[[The Battle at Lake Changjin]]'' to become the [[List of highest-grossing non-English films|highest-grossing non-English language film]]. It became the 57th film overall, and 14th animated film to pass $1{{nbsp}}billion and the seventh film to pass $2{{nbsp}}billion.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ramachandran |first=Naman |date=2025-02-07 |title='Ne Zha 2' Torches Box Office Records, Becomes Highest-Grossing Chinese Film Ever |url=https://variety.com/2025/film/news/ne-zha-2-china-box-office-1236300222/ |access-date=2025-02-19 |website=Variety}}</ref> It became the [[List of highest-grossing animated films|highest-grossing animated film]] of all time as well as the [[List of highest-grossing films|5th highest-grossing film overall]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-02-19 |title=China's 'Ne Zha 2' beats 'Inside Out 2' with $1.72 BILLION box office collection; crowned highest-grossing animated film of all time |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/english/hollywood/box-office/chinas-ne-zha-2-beats-inside-out-2-with-1-72-billion-haul-crowned-highest-grossing-animated-film-of-all-time/articleshow/118371077.cms |access-date=2025-02-19 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref> It became the second ever non-Hollywood film production to become the highest-grossing film of the year, following ''[[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – The Movie: Mugen Train|Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Mugen Train]]'' in [[2020 in film|2020]] during the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].
** It surpassed ''[[Inside Out 2]]'' (2024) as the highest-grossing animated film,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gearan |first=Hannah |date=2025-02-18 |title=Inside Out 2 Dethroned As Highest-Grossing Animated Movie Of All Time |url=https://screenrant.com/ne-zha-2-movie-box-office-inside-out-2-highest-grossing-animated-movie-all-time/ |access-date=2025-02-19 |website=Screen Rant}}</ref> breaking [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]]'s 14-year streak with the title after regaining it with ''[[Toy Story 3]]'' (2010). Doing so, [[Beijing Enlight Pictures|Enlight Pictures]] became the first non-Hollywood studio to hold this distinction.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hood |first=Cooper |date=2023-12-25 |title=Every Highest-Grossing Animated Movie & How Long It Held The Record |url=https://screenrant.com/every-highest-grossing-animated-movie-how-long/#:~:text=Animated%20movies%20have%20a%20long,grossing%20movies%20of%20the%20year. |access-date=2025-02-19 |website=Screen Rant}}</ref>
** It became the first non-English language film to gross $1{{nbsp}}billion and $2{{nbsp}}billion worldwide.<ref name="$1 Billion">{{cite news |last1=Tartaglione |first1=Nancy |title='Ne Zha 2' Crosses $1B At China Box Office; First Movie Ever To Milestone In A Single Market |url=https://deadline.com/2025/02/ne-zha-2-box-office-china-1236281764/ |access-date=9 February 2025 |website=Deadline Hollywood |date=9 February 2025}}</ref>
** It surpassed ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'' to become the highest-grossing film ever in a single market.<ref name="$1 Billion" /> It also became the first film to earn $1{{nbsp}}billion and $2{{nbsp}}billion in a single market.<ref name="$1 Billion" />
** On March 2, thirty-three days after release, ''[[Ne Zha 2]]'' surpassed $2{{nbsp}}billion, the first animated film in history to do so. It is the seventh film overall to achieve this milestone.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Malhotra |first=Rahul |date=2025-03-02 |title=China's 'Ne Zha 2' Is the First Animated Movie To Pass $2 Billion at the Global Box Office |url=https://collider.com/ne-zha-2-global-box-office-2-billion/ |access-date=2025-03-02 |website=Collider}}</ref>
** It set the records of [[List of highest-grossing openings for animated films#Biggest worldwide openings for an animated film since 2002|highest-grossing worldwide opening for an animated film]] and highest-grossing worldwide opening of the year, up until these records were surpassed by ''Zootopia 2'' later the same year.<ref name="Z2_BoxOfficeRecords" />
* ''[[Zootopia 2]]'' became the 59th film overall, the 15th animated film, and the [[List of fastest-grossing films#Fastest to $1 billion|second-fastest animated film]] (at 17 days, behind ''Ne Zha 2''’s 12 days)<ref>{{Cite web|last=Fuster|first=Jeremy|date=12 December 2025|title='Zootopia 2' Hits Record $1 Billion in Just 17 Days|url=https://www.thewrap.com/zootopia-2-hits-1-billion-box-office/|access-date=5 January 2026|publisher=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref> to gross $1 billion worldwide. 
** It claimed the [[List of highest-grossing openings for films#Biggest worldwide openings on record|fourth highest-grossing worldwide opening]] of all time ($560.3{{nbsp}}million),<ref>{{Cite web|last=Hughes|first=Mark|date=30 November 2025|title='Zootopia 2' 4th-Biggest Box Office Debut In History, Biggest 2025 Weekend|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/markhughes/2025/11/30/zootopia-2-4th-biggest-box-office-debut-in-history-biggest-2025-weekend/|access-date=3 December 2025|work=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> placing behind ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' ($1.2{{nbsp}}billion),<ref>{{Cite web|last=McClintock|first=Pamela|date=28 April 2019|title='Avengers: Endgame' Box Office: All the Records Broken in $1.2B Global, It’s also the fastest grossing pg rated movie and the fastest pg rated movie to hit 1B, Bow|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/avengers-endgame-box-office-all-records-broken-12b-bow-1205398/|access-date=3 December 2025|publisher=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> ''[[Avengers: Infinity War]]'' ($641{{nbsp}}million),<ref>{{Cite web|last=Mendelson|first=Scott|date=29 April 2018|title=Box Office: 'Avengers: Infinity War' Assembles Record $641M Debut|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/scottmendelson/2018/04/29/avengers-infinity-war-destroys-box-office-records-with-630m-global-bow/|access-date=3 December 2025|work=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> and ''[[Spider-Man: No Way Home]]'' ($601{{nbsp}}million).<ref>{{Cite web|last=Tartaglione|first=Nancy|date=20 December 2021|title='Spider-Man: No Way Home' Is Even More Amazing With $601M Global Debut For 3rd Biggest WW Bow Ever; $341M Snared Overseas – International Box Office|url=https://deadline.com/2021/12/spider-man-no-way-home-global-opening-records-matrix-international-box-office-1234899298/|access-date=3 December 2025|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref>
** It set the records of [[List of highest-grossing openings for animated films#Biggest worldwide openings for an animated film since 2002|highest-grossing worldwide opening for an animated film]],<ref>{{Cite web|last=Welsh|first=Oli|date=30 November 2025|title=Zootopia 2 opens to record-breaking box office — thanks to China|url=https://www.polygon.com/zootopia-2-box-office-china/|access-date=3 December 2025|publisher=[[Polygon (website)|Polygon]]}}</ref> and highest-grossing worldwide opening of the year,<ref name="Z2_TWDCPress">{{Cite web|date=30 November 2025|title='Zootopia 2' Roars to Record-Breaking Global Box Office Opening|url=https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/zootopia-2-box-office-disney/|access-date=3 December 2025|publisher=[[The Walt Disney Company]]}}</ref> surpassing ''Ne Zha 2'' in both instances.<ref name="Z2_BoxOfficeRecords">{{Cite web|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=30 November 2025|title='Zootopia 2' – All The Box Office Records Broken|url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/zootopia-2-box-office-records-1236631348/|access-date=3 December 2025|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref> It is also the highest-grossing worldwide opening of any animated film in [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] history,<ref name="Z2_TWDCPress" /> surpassing ''[[Moana 2]]''.<ref name="Z2_BoxOfficeRecords" />
** On 12 December, seventeen days after release, ''[[Zootopia 2]]'' became the fastest [[Motion Picture Association|MPA]] animated film,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Tartaglione|first=Nancy|date=12 December 2025|title=Money Bunny! 'Zootopia 2' Crossing $1 Billion Global Box Office Today; Fastest Hollywood Animation Ever To Milestone|url=https://deadline.com/2025/12/zootopia-2-1-billion-global-box-office-milestone-1236647067/|access-date=15 December 2025|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref> and [[Motion Picture Association film rating system#MPA film ratings|PG-rated]] film,<ref>{{Cite web|last=McClintock|first=Pamela|date=14 December 2025|title=Global Box Office: 'Zootopia 2' Gobbles Up $1B Faster Than Any PG-Rated Film in History|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/zootopia-2-box-office-zooms-past-1-billion-1236448881/|access-date=15 December 2025|publisher=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> to reach $1{{nbsp}}billion, surpassing ''[[Inside Out 2]]''’s 19 days in both instances.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Murray|first=Conor|date=12 December 2025|title=Disney's 'Zootopia 2' Breaks Another Record: Becomes The Fastest Animated Movie To Cross This Box Office Figure|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/conormurray/2025/12/12/disneys-zootopia-2-breaks-another-record-becomes-the-fastest-animated-movie-to-cross-this-box-office-figure/|access-date=15 December 2025|publisher=[[Forbes]]}}</ref>
** On 31 December, thirty-six days after release, ''[[Zootopia 2]]'' surpassed ''[[Frozen 2]]'' to become [[Walt Disney Animation Studios#Highest-grossing films|Walt Disney Animation Studios' highest-grossing film]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=31 December 2025|title='Zootopia 2' Bests 'Frozen 2' To Become Highest-Grossing Walt Disney Animation Title Of All Time|url=https://deadline.com/2025/12/zootopia-2-box-office-walt-disney-record-1236659242/|access-date=5 January 2026|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref>
** On 18 January, fifty-four days after release, ''[[Zootopia 2]]'' surpassed ''[[Inside Out 2]]'' to become [[Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures#Highest-grossing films|Disney's highest-grossing animated film]] of all time,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Julian|first=Mark|date=18 January 2026|title=ZOOTOPIA 2 Definitively Becomes Disney's Highest Grossing Animated Film Of All-Time|url=https://toonado.com/movies/zootopia-2-definitively-becomes-disneys-highest-grossing-animated-film-of-all-time-a10087|access-date=19 January 2026|publisher=Toonado}}</ref> the [[List of highest-grossing animated films#Highest-grossing animated films|highest-grossing MPA animated film]] of all time,<ref name="Z2_TWDCPress2">{{Cite web|date=18 January 2026|title='Zootopia 2' Becomes the Highest-Grossing Animated MPA Film of All Time Globally|url=https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/news/zootopia-2-highest-grossing-animated-film/|access-date=19 January 2026|publisher=[[The Walt Disney Company]]}}</ref> and the [[List of highest-grossing films#Highest-grossing films|highest-grossing PG-rated film]] of all time.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Top Lifetime Grosses by MPA Rating (PG; Worldwide)|url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/chart/mpaa_title_lifetime_gross/?area=XWW&by_mpaa=PG|access-date=19 January 2026|publisher=[[Box Office Mojo]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=All Time Worldwide Box Office for PG Movies|url=https://www.the-numbers.com/box-office-records/worldwide/all-movies/mpaa-ratings/pg-(us)|access-date=22 February 2026|publisher=[[The Numbers (website)|The Numbers]]}}</ref>
** The ''[[Zootopia (franchise)|Zootopia]]'' film franchise surpassed $2.8{{nbsp}}billion with the release of ''Zootopia 2''.<ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Zootopia (2016)|id=2948356/|access-date=15 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Zootopia 2 (2025)|id=26443597/|access-date=15 December 2025}}</ref>
* ''[[Avatar: Fire and Ash]]'' became the 60th film overall to gross $1{{nbsp}}billion worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Lang|first=Robert|date=5 January 2026|title=The Movies That Have Made More Than $1 Billion At The Global Box Office|url=https://deadline.com/gallery/highest-grossing-movies-all-time/avatar-from-left-zoe-saldana-sam-worthington-2009-tm-copyright-20th-century-fox-all-rights/|access-date=5 January 2026|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref>
** The ''[[Avatar (franchise)|Avatar]]'' film series surpassed $6{{nbsp}}billion with the release of ''Avatar: Fire and Ash''.<ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Avatar (2009)|id=0499549/|access-date=5 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Avatar: The Way of Water (2022)|id=1630029/|access-date=5 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Avatar: Fire and Ash (2025)|id=1757678/|access-date=5 January 2026}}</ref>
** It became the first film in the franchise to not reach $2 billion at the box office.
* ''[[Lilo & Stitch (2025 film)|Lilo & Stitch]]'' became the 58th film overall,<ref>{{cite web|title=Lilo & Stitch Becomes First 2025 Title to Cross $1 Billion Globally|date=17 July 2025|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/lilo-and-stitch-becomes-first-billion-box-office-1236318553/|publisher=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> and the first [[Motion Picture Association|MPA]] film of 2025 to gross $1{{nbsp}}billion worldwide.<ref>{{cite web |title='Lilo & Stitch' Becomes First $1 Billion MPA Film of 2025 at the Global Box Office|date=17 July 2025|url=https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/lilo-stitch-1-billion-box-office/|publisher=[[The Walt Disney Company]]}}</ref>
** It became the second best first-day ticket pre-seller for a Disney [[List of remakes and adaptations of Disney animated films|live-action remake]], behind the 2019 photorealistic animated ''[[The Lion King (2019 film)|The Lion King]]''.<ref name="deadline.com">{{cite web|title='Lilo & Stitch' Presales Ahead of 'A Minecraft Movie'; Best First Day for PG Title YTD|date=7 May 2025|url=https://deadline.com/2025/05/lilo-stitch-box-office-advance-ticket-sales-1236388406/|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref>
** It also set the record for the [[List of highest-grossing live-action/animated films#Opening weekends|biggest opening weekend for a live-action animated film]], surpassing ''[[Detective Pikachu (film)|Detective Pikachu]]''.<ref>{{cite web|title='Lilo & Stitch' Surfs To Galactic $341.7M Global Opening; 'Mission: Impossible – Final Reckoning' Lights The Fuse With Franchise-Best $204M WW Launch – International Box Office|date=25 May 2025|url=https://deadline.com/2025/05/lilo-stitch-mission-impossible-box-office-global-opening-international-1236409506/|publisher=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title='Pokemon Detective Pikachu' beats 'Avengers: Endgame' by a whisker at international box office|date=12 May 2009|url=https://www.screendaily.com/box-office/pokemon-detective-pikachu-beats-avengers-endgame-by-a-whisker-at-international-box-office/5139276.article/|publisher=[[Screen International|ScreenDaily]]}}</ref>
** It became the [[List of highest-grossing live-action/animated films#Highest-grossing live-action animated films|highest-grossing live-action animated film]], surpassing ''[[The Smurfs (film)|The Smurfs]]'' (2011), as well as the first live-action animated film to globally gross at least $1{{nbsp}}billion.<ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=The Smurfs (2011)|id=0472181|access-date=August 16, 2025}}</ref><ref name="L&S_25_BO">{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Lilo & Stitch (2025)|id=11655566/|access-date=August 16, 2025}}</ref>
** The ''[[Lilo & Stitch (franchise)|Lilo & Stitch]]'' film series has grossed more than $1.3{{nbsp}}billion with the release of the live-action remake, with the latter contributing roughly 79% of that figure.<ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=Lilo & Stitch (2002)|id=0275847|access-date=August 16, 2025}}</ref><ref name="L&S_25_BO" />
*''[[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – The Movie: Infinity Castle|Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle]]'' grossed about $820.4{{nbsp}}million worldwide to become the [[List of highest-grossing Japanese films|highest-grossing Japanese film of all time]], surpassing its predecessor ''[[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – The Movie: Mugen Train|Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Mugen Train]]''.
**Worldwide, it became the highest-grossing Japanese film and the [[Highest-grossing anime films|highest-grossing anime film]] of all time.<ref name="CrunchyrollInfinity">{{Cite web |last=Harding |first=Daryl |date=September 24, 2025 |title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle Becomes Highest-Grossing Anime Film Worldwide |url=https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2025/9/23/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-infinity-castle-highest-grossing-anime-film-worldwide |access-date=September 24, 2025 |website=[[Crunchyroll News]]}}</ref> It is also the first Japanese film to cross $800{{nbsp}}million worldwide.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2025-09-28 |title=Demon Slayer -Kimetsu no Yaiba- The Movie: Infinity Castle (2025) |url=https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba-The-Movie-Infinity-Castle-(2025-Japan) |access-date=2025-10-26 |website=The Numbers |language=en-US}}</ref>
**In Japan, it had the biggest opening weekend of all time with ¥5.52{{nbsp}}billion in three days.<ref name="Slayer">{{Cite web |last=Harding |first=Daryl |date=2025-07-22 |title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle First Movie Breaks 3 Japan Box Office Opening Weekend Records |url=https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2025/7/22/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-infinity-castle-first-movie-breaks-3-japan-box-office-opening-weekend-records |access-date=2025-07-26 |website=Crunchyroll |language=en}}</ref> It passed ¥10{{nbsp}}billion in eight days, becoming the fastest‑grossing film ever in Japan.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-07-27 |title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle Film Breaks Records in 10 Days |url=https://us.oricon-group.com/news/5536/ |access-date=2025-07-27 |website=Oricon |language=en}}</ref>
**In the [[United States|US]], its $70{{nbsp}}million opening weekend was the biggest opening for an international film, R‑rated animated film,<ref name="THRInfinity">{{Cite web |last=McClintock |first=Pamela |date=2025-09-14 |title=Box Office: Anime 'Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle' Makes History With Record $70M U.S. Opening |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-record-box-office-opening-1236370035/ |access-date=2025-09-24 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> and September animated release.<ref name="THRInfinity" /> It went on to set US records for the highest-grossing anime film (surpassing ''[[Pokémon: The First Movie]]''), highest-grossing Japanese film,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tassi |first=Paul |date=September 22, 2025 |title='Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle' Just Broke Three Huge Box Office Records |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2025/09/22/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-just-broke-three-huge-box-office-records/ |access-date=2025-09-24 |website=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> first anime film to cross $100{{nbsp}}million,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Malhotra |first=Rahul |date=2025-10-05 |title=Michael Bay's Franchise-Killing Flop Gets Slain by 2025's Biggest Surprise Hit |url=https://collider.com/demon-slayer-infinity-train-overtakes-michael-bay-transformers-the-last-knight-box-office-620-million/ |access-date=2025-10-05 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]}}</ref> and highest-grossing international film (surpassing ''[[Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon]]'').<ref>{{Cite web |last=McClintock |first=Pamela |date=2025-10-12 |title=Box Office: 'Tron' Hits the Skids With $33.5M Opening, 'Roofman' No. 2 at $8M |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/tron-hits-the-skids-box-office-opening-1236398953/ |access-date=2025-10-12 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref>
**In other international markets, the film had the biggest opening weekend for an animated film in the Philippines, South Korea,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bagchi |first=Nillohit |date=2025-08-26 |title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle breaks more records around the globe, overtakes Avengers Endgame with $7.4M pre-sales in South Korea |url=https://poprant.indiatimes.com/trending/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-breaks-more-records-around-the-globe-overtakes-avengers-endgame-with-74m-pre-sales-in-south-korea-667893.html |access-date=2025-09-27 |website=[[Indiatimes.com]] |language=en-IN}}</ref> and India.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Singh |first=Jatinder |date=2025-09-15 |title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Infinity Castle Opens to 48cr in India, Biggest Ever for an Animated film |url=https://www.pinkvilla.com/entertainment/box-office/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-opens-to-48cr-weekend-in-india-biggest-ever-for-a-animated-film-1396858 |access-date=2025-09-27 |website=[[Pinkvilla]]}}</ref> It became the all-time highest-grossing anime film in Brazil, [[Hong Kong]], India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Mexico, Philippines, Spain, and Thailand.<ref name="CrunchyrollInfinity" />
**The ''[[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba]]'' franchise became the first R-rated animated film series to surpass $1{{nbsp}}billion with the release of ''[[Infinity Castle]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Alt |first=Matt |date=June 18, 2021 |title="Demon Slayer": The Viral Blockbuster from Japan |url=https://www.newyorker.com/culture/cultural-comment/demon-slayer-the-viral-blockbuster-from-japan |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210619223831/https://www.newyorker.com/culture/cultural-comment/demon-slayer-the-viral-blockbuster-from-japan |archive-date=June 19, 2021 |access-date=June 20, 2021 |magazine=[[The New Yorker]]}}</ref>
**It became the [[List of highest-grossing animated films#Traditional animation|highest-grossing hand drawn animated film]] in its initial release, surpassing the initial gross of ''[[The Lion King]]'' (1994), which grossed $763{{nbsp}}million in its initial release and held the record for 31 years.{{cn|date=January 2026}}
* The ''[[How to Train Your Dragon]]'' franchise surpassed $2{{nbsp}}billion with the release of the live-action remake of the same name. It became the highest grossing film in the franchise, surpassing [[How to Train Your Dragon 2]].<ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=How to Train Your Dragon (2010)|id=0892769/|access-date=14 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=How to Train Your Dragon 2 (2014)|id=1646971/|access-date=14 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=How to Train Your Dragon: The Hidden World (2019)|id=2386490/|access-date=14 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite Box Office Mojo|title=How to Train Your Dragon (2025)|id=26743210/|access-date=14 December 2025}}</ref>
* ''[[F1 (film)|F1]]'' achieved [[Apple Studios]]'s highest-grossing opening weekend at $144{{nbsp}}million worldwide,<ref>{{cite news|url=https://variety.com/2025/film/box-office/brad-pitt-f1-movie-box-office-record-apple-megan-2-flops-1236443608/|title=Brad Pitt's 'F1' Delivers Apple's First Box Office Hit With $55.6 Million Debut, 'M3GAN 2.0' Fizzles With $10 Million|first=Rebecca|last=Rubin|publisher=Variety|date=June 29, 2025|accessdate=June 29, 2025}}</ref> and passed ''[[Napoleon (2023 film)|Napoleon]]'' to become the producer's highest-grossing film worldwide.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2025/film/box-office/jurassic-world-rebirth-opening-weekend-box-office-july-4th-holiday-weekend-1236448064/|title=Box Office: 'Jurassic World Rebirth' Stomps to $147 Million Over July Fourth Holiday Weekend|first=Rebecca|last=Rubin|website=Variety|date=July 6, 2025|accessdate=July 6, 2025}}</ref>
* The ''[[Superman in film|Superman]]'' film series surpassed $3{{nbsp}}billion with the release of ''[[Superman (2025 film)|Superman]]''.{{cn|date=November 2025}}
* The [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] became the first [[film franchise]] to gross $32{{nbsp}}billion with the releases of ''[[Captain America: Brave New World]]'', ''[[Thunderbolts*]]'', and ''[[The Fantastic Four: First Steps]]''.{{cn|date=December 2025}}

